    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0446" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg376"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 196.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch (No. 176) of the 24th ultimo, accompanied by a copy of your letter of
                    the 15th ultimo to our consul at Marseilles in regard to the case of one
                    Gauthreaux, a destitute citizen of the United States, and to the support of
                    paupers from the United States in foreign countries and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >vice versa</hi>. The views expressed in that letter are entirely
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
